{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>You shall be.</b> Officer over my house." "<b>ישק.</b> The dagesh in the shin is for the missing nun of נשק, and it means commander of the army. Others say it is from the root נשיקה (kissing) by a remote derivation." "<b>Only the throne אגדל from you.</b> It is known that אגדל is a participle, and its meaning is: I shall have nothing greater than you, only the greatness of the throne. And \"כי מנעורי גדלני כאב\" (Job 31:18) is not a transitive verb; rather its meaning is \"great with me.\" And the construction of \"אגדל ממך\" in Scripture is well known, like \"נובלת עליה\" (Isaiah 1:30), \"ותאבדו דרך\" (Psalms 2:12)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:45.568995978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}